{"id": "1541654525826306088", "channel_id": "1541375063792549918", "author_id": "169824455231537152", "author_name": ".dyrnwyn", "content": "When they announced it I was under the impression thast every instance of doing the things (Arith use, Exalt, cards played etc.) was going to contribute to everyone's affinity. The numbers are so low that even if they made the affinity for doing things universal it would STILL barely be comparable to the old system on longer missions. As it is though, main DPS are getting like half of the old affinity gain per mission at best, and supports that don't use as many cards likely aren't even getting 1/4th of the old gain even on longer missions. It's absurd that even if you're bringing a character on missions they STILL aren't getting any affinity if their kit doesn't allow for it", "timestamp": "2026-08-25T03:44:41.513000+00:00", "thread_id": "1541375063792549918", "edited_timestamp": "2026-08-25T03:45:28.551000+00:00", "thread_title": "Impact of Version 2.6 Affinity Changes on Player Experience", "forum_channel_id": "1180845276823564288", "thread_tags": ["1181168158678204497", "1361168939622727801"]}
